# Optional review summarization. User requested postponing provider configuration on 2026-10-22.
# Keep disabled until an authorized provider, model and server-side credential are supplied.
KG_REVIEW_AI_ENABLED=false
KG_REVIEW_AI_ENDPOINT=
KG_REVIEW_AI_API_KEY=
KG_REVIEW_AI_MODEL=
KG_REVIEW_AI_DAILY_LIMIT=30
KG_REVIEW_AI_HOURLY_LIMIT=5

# ENDPOINT must be a complete HTTPS URL ending in /chat/completions.
# The provider must support model/messages, response_format=json_object,
# max_completion_tokens, stream=false and store=false. No automatic provider fallback.
# Keep API_KEY in the server's protected service environment, never in the repository,
# client .env, admin panel responses, shell history or release artifacts.
# Reconfigure/restart the service using the established release procedure.
# Missing or invalid configuration => ai.status=disabled, score=null.
# A scheduler runs after 120 seconds and once/minute, on a separate bounded worker.
# Public detail/reviews GETs read a cache only and do not invoke the provider.
# Global Redis atomic budget: 30 calls/day, 5/hour by default; each stay once/hour.
# Hard configuration ceilings: 100/day, 10/hour; HTTP deadline at most 30 seconds.
# Each call uses at most 120 latest public reviews linked to a completed stay order,
# at most 16 room types and 400 characters per review. Known guest names, phone,
# email/contact identifiers and URLs are redacted; user/order IDs and media are not sent.
# AI outputs are strict JSON with 1-5 scores, bounded text and in-scope evidence indices.
# A failed/invalid generation is unavailable for an hour, without invented AI fallback.
# Successful cache lasts seven days; a changed/deleted/hidden review invalidates it
# immediately on read by input fingerprint. Output is checked against current input
# again before saving. Cache/budget Redis failures fail closed.
# API: detail.ai, detail.roomTypes[].ai, room-types[].ai,
# reviews/summary.ai and reviews/summary.roomTypes[].ai. Existing avg/rating unchanged.
# status: ready / pending / disabled / unavailable / no_reviews / not_in_sample.
# Only ready has source=model, score, summary, highlights, cautions, generatedAt.
# reviewCount is the analyzed sample size, not the whole historical review count.
# not_in_sample means room reviews exist but are outside the current bounded sample.
# Users should see 'AI参考分，不替代住客评分' and separate actual guest rating statistics.
# Official protocol: https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/resources/chat/subresources/completions/methods/create
